on't  be leaders we will continue to benchmark  and we will do this mid-pack that was  the exact language used with this mid  path we felt defeated it became apparent  that through the grapevine that they  were going to be offering insurance for  pets and I thought I was gonna die  there's no way my company can make a  mistake like that to cover pets and not  cover children  [Music]  back then I was the one senior manager  foods now so there were people who did a  lot more for gay right the tractor who  really worked it worked so hard and I  can't say that I did I just was trying  to stay alive most of the time I wasn't  looking for people's approval I was just  looking for accepted all I wanted a  level playing field let me do good work  and judge me fairly I'll remember I got  a call from someone who at that time I  didn't know and his name was Gary right  and he came to my office as he said he  wanted to do or to talk about a subject  of diversity and he came and he had a  couple of folks with him who I can  hardly remember but I certainly remember  Gary he said John I know you're very  committed to diversity that's obvious to  us all but you need to know that there  is a huge outage in the way you're  approaching diversity in this company  well that got my attention and what he  said he was talking about was that we  were not recognizing a different way of  life in front of employees  now Susan Arnold was a very important  person to me  with the company Susan and I have worked  together in different parts of the soap  business for years and I never really  thought about her marital or personal  life one way or the other and I really  hadn't sat down with her and had a kind  of conversation that who are you what is  but your whole life like well there was  a one of these dividend days and I saw  Susan across the way and she was sitting  there with two young children and their  partner it came together for me in a  particular way because I knew Susan in  so many d